# Implementation Plan - ONION AI Agent for Home Page

Create and integrate **ONION**, an AI-powered Security Operations Center (SOC) Assistant and Threat Monitoring Agent, directly on the application's home page (Dashboard). ONION will answer user queries, analyze system security metrics, explain ransomware detection telemetry, recommend security postures, and execute direct actions.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **ONION AI Agent Capabilities**:
> ONION will operate with real-time access to database metrics (anomaly scores, active alerts, host detector status, whitelisted processes, and log telemetry).
> It will feature a hybrid smart AI engine capable of answering domain-specific cybersecurity & platform questions out-of-the-box, with support for live LLM response enrichment if API credentials are configured.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Logic

#### [MODIFY] [backend/app.py](file:///d:/HACK-LEARNATHONS/LEARNATHON%20SLOT%203/FINAL/PRO/PRO/backend/app.py)
- Implement `/api/onion/chat` endpoint:
  - Accepts user prompt, `user_id`, and session context.
  - Queries active alerts, anomaly score, process whitelist count, and detector ping state to inject real-time security context.
  - Processes queries using ONION's specialized SOC AI engine (supporting threat status checks, ransomware pre-encryption explanations, log summaries, whitelist info, security recommendations, and general queries).
  - Returns structured AI responses containing markdown text, action suggestions, and interactive security trigger buttons.
- Implement `/api/onion/diagnose` endpoint for quick automated SOC system health diagnostics.

